# The reference captures are raw bytes: `cargo xtask reference verify` hashes
# them, and a CRLF-converting checkout must never rewrite them.
reference/**/*.rgb binary
reference/**/*.idx binary
# The demo's media are read as raw bytes too, and several (PAM/OUT.ANI, the PLZPART .INC tables,
# the U2A scene files) hold no NUL in their first 8 KB, so git would take them for text and a
# CRLF-converting checkout — Windows' default — would corrupt them. `cargo xtask assets verify
# --tree` checks them against assets/PROVENANCE.md.
assets/** -text
